<article class="env-lemma" id="EC884A">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/EC884A">Lemma <span data-tag="EC884A">3.2.4.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a simplicial set, $\calC $ a simplicial category, and $\phi : \sCoNerve [S] \rightarrow \calC ^{op}$ a simplicial functor. The following are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The Quillen adjunction $( St^{+}_{\phi }, Un^{+}_{\phi } )$ is a Quillen equivalence. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
The functor $Un^{+}_{\phi }$ induces an equivalence of simplicial categories 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  (Un^{+}_{\phi })^{\circ } : ((\mSet )^{\calC })^{\circ } \rightarrow ((\mSet )_{/S})^{\circ }, \]
</div>
<p>
 where $((\mSet )^{\calC })^{\circ }$ denotes the full (simplicial) subcategory of $( ( \mSet )^{\calC })$ consisting of fibrant-cofibrant objects, and $((\mSet )_{/S})^{\circ }$ denotes the full (simplicial) subcategory of $(\mSet )_{/S}$ consisting of fibrant-cofibrant objects. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>